== links natural n=65536 valuesFor: ordered vs btree-sets
A: 497.8 ns per operation (median)
B: 943.2 ns per operation (median)
A needs 47% less time than B: B takes 1.89 times as long as A.
With 95% confidence the difference lies between 45.2% and 48.7% less time (B takes between 1.83 and 1.95 times as long as A).
Noise floor: 1.34%. Identical code measured against itself on this setup can look that different, so smaller differences mean nothing.
Neighbouring measurements are nearly independent (autocorrelation -0.28), so they were resampled one by one.

Verdict: RESOLVED. A is faster than B: the difference is real, as its interval excludes zero and it exceeds the noise floor.

Warnings:
  - the program holds 671 MB of live data, more than the caches of many machines; for data that size, where it lies in memory can shift the result by several points in ways the interval does not cover, and differently in the next process; run the comparison in several processes with the multiproc package

